FINAL ANSWER:
**Top author holds 59.5% of surviving lines (869 of 1,460 non-blank lines). Fatih Arslan is the single point of concentration.**

**Bus factor (scope: whole repo at HEAD, 11 files):**
- Bus factor 1: Fatih Arslan alone holds 59.5% of 1,460 non-blank lines. Counting blank lines (1,824 attributed), he holds 61.7%.
- To reach 80%: 6 authors on non-blank lines, 5 counting blank lines.
- This measures how concentrated the surviving code is. It does not measure who understands it.

**Ranking (surviving lines, non-blank; commit share in brackets):**

| # | Author | Lines | Share | Commits | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Fatih Arslan | 869 | 59.5% | 80 (57.6%) | 2026-03-20 |
| 2 | Linda_pp | 111 | 7.6% | 1 (0.7%) | 2017-05-23 |
| 3 | Matthew Hall | 84 | 5.8% | 1 (0.7%) | 2026-03-04 |
| 4 | Greg Poirson | 49 | 3.4% | 7 (5.0%) | 2023-10-17 |
| 5 | Alex Guerrieri | 46 | 3.2% | 1 (0.7%) | 2015-10-26 |
| 6 | Albert | 44 | 3.0% | 3 (2.2%) | 2016-10-19 |
| 7 | Robert Pająk | 41 | 2.8% | 4 (2.9%) | 2023-03-01 |
| 8 | Cameron Moore | 40 | 2.7% | 1 (0.7%) | 2016-09-27 |
| 9 | Andrew Austin | 37 | 2.5% | 1 (0.7%) | 2015-08-23 |
| 10 | Klaus Post | 28 | 1.9% | 1 (0.7%) | 2024-04-08 |
| 11 | majiayu000 | 24 | 1.6% | 1 (0.7%) | 2026-01-01 |
| 12 | Thimo | 15 | 1.0% | 1 (0.7%) | 2014-11-26 |

Tail: 32 more authors hold 4.9% together; largest is Martin Lindhe at 0.9%.

Beyond Fatih, no one holds more than 7.6%. Ownership below him is spread thin. Most of the other authors wrote one commit that still survives.

**Identities:** Greg Poirson (also listed as `greg`) and Albert (also listed as `bogem`) are each one address under two names, already counted as one person. No `.mailmap` exists, so these merges come from the tool's identity logic and are not written anywhere. Nothing else was merged.

**What was left out:**
- Bots: `dependabot[bot]` excluded, 7 lines and 38 commits removed.
- Dropped files: 4 files, 237 lines. That is `vendor` (2 files, 128 lines), `attribute_string.go` (generated, 103 lines), and `go.sum` (6 lines).
- Reformat commit ignored: `4831a13` ("all: use any instead of interface{}"), listed in `.git-blame-ignore-revs` as a `gofmt -r` rewrite.
- Mechanical-rewrite check: 97 commits examined, 0 set aside. One more looks mechanical but was not set aside: `52aa0a6` (typo fix `fmt.Ffprintf` → `fmt.Fprintf`, 1 surviving line). It does not change the picture.

**Copy detection:** Figures use `git blame -w -M -C`. Without `-C`, Fatih is at 56.6% (827 lines), 2.9 points lower. Raj Patel moves from 0.2% (3 lines) with copy detection to 6.0% (88 lines) without, a shift of more than 2 points. Raj is not in the top 12. Alex Guerrieri moves from 3.2% to 1.6%, under 2 points.

**Limits:** This shows survivorship, not quality. Review, design docs, and deleted code are not counted. Fatih's last commit was 2026-03-20, about seven months before today, so the concentration is in code he wrote, not in recent activity.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | grep -v '^vendor/' | grep -E '\.go$' | wc -l && git ls-files | grep -c '^vendor/' ; git ls-files | grep -v '^vendor/' | grep -E '\.go$' | xargs -I{} git blame --line-porcelain -w -- {} 2>/dev/null | grep -E '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
 - Bash: git log --format='%an' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head; echo ---; git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort -u | wc -l; echo ---; git ls-files | grep -v '^vendor/' | wc -l; cat .git-blame-ignore-revs 2>/dev/null | head -5
 - Bash: git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$'; echo ---; git ls-files | grep '^vendor/'; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$'); do echo "$f: $(git blame --line-porcelain -w -- "$f" | grep -E '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3 | tr -s ' ' | tr '\n' ';')"; done; echo ---; git blame --line-porcelain -w -- $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$') | grep -E '^author ' | wc -l
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$' | grep -v '^vendor/'); do git blame --line-porcelain -w -- "$f"; done | grep -E '^author ' | sed 's/^author //' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn > /tmp/own.txt; cat /tmp/own.txt; awk '{s+=$1} END {print "total", s}' /tmp/own.txt; echo ---; git blame --line-porcelain -w -- vendor/github.com/mattn/go-isatty/isatty_tcgets.go | grep -c '^author '; echo ---; git log --format='%an' -- $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$' | grep -v '^vendor/') | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -5; echo; git log --format='%an' -- . | sort -u | wc -l
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$' | grep -v '^vendor/'); do git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs --line-porcelain -w -- "$f"; done | grep -E '^author ' | sed 's/^author //' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -6; echo; git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs --line-porcelain -w -- $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$' | grep -v '^vendor/') | grep -E '^author ' | wc -l; git log --format=%an | wc -l; git log --format=%an | grep -v dependabot | wc -l
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files | grep -E '\.go$' | grep -v '^vendor/'); do git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs --line-porcelain -w -- "$f"; done | grep -E '^author ' | wc -l; git log --format=%an | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | awk '{s+=$1} END {print s}'
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Fatih Arslan owns about half the live code. The next person, Linda_pp, owns under 9%.

Live code here is 6 non-vendor Go files, 1,657 surviving lines (`git blame`, whitespace ignored, honoring `.git-blame-ignore-revs`):

| Rank | Author | Live lines | Share |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Fatih Arslan | 823 | 49.7% |
| 2 | Linda_pp | 144 | 8.7% |
| 3 | Lena Hoffmann | 103 | 6.2% |
| 4 | Matthew Hall | 98 | 5.9% |
| 5 | Raj Patel | 97 | 5.9% |
| 6 | Cameron Moore | 50 | 3.0% |

Fatih's lines sit mostly in `color.go`, `color_test.go`, and `doc.go`, the core of the library. Fatih also made 201 of 300 commits (about 67%). 38 of the 300 are dependabot.

Caveats:
- Without the blame-ignore file, Fatih is 48.2% and Raj is second at 9.8%. The ranking after Fatih shifts, but the picture doesn't.
- Blame counts surviving lines, not who understands the code. The codebase is small, so one person's share swings a lot.
- The one vendored file (`vendor/.../isatty_tcgets.go`) is upstream code, so I excluded it. It is not a measure of the maintainers.

For bus-factor purposes, a single maintainer holds about half the code and most of the history. Given the small size, a few people reading through the core files would cover most of the risk.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Skill: {"skill": "tool:skill", "args": "Assess ownership concentration of the code that is live in this repo today (files at HEAD, not deleted history). Report the share of the top author and the ranking of the next authors. Use git history from the current HEAD only."}
 - Bash: git ls-files | wc -l && git rev-list --count HEAD && git log --format='%ae' HEAD | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
 - Bash: git ls-files | sed 's|/[^/]*$||' | sort | uniq -c; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep '^author-mail ' ; done | sed 's/^author-mail //' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn > /tmp/blame_all.txt; cat /tmp/blame_all.txt; echo ---; awk '{s+=$1} END {print "total lines", s}' /tmp/blame_all.txt
 - Bash: git ls-files -s vendor; cat .gitmodules 2>/dev/null; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files | grep -v '^vendor'); do n=$(git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" | grep -c '^author-mail'); echo "$n $f"; done; echo ---; git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- $(git ls-files | grep -v '^vendor') | grep '^author-mail ' | sed 's/^author-mail //' | grep -v dependabot | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | awk '{s+=$1; a[NR]=$0} END {for(i=1;i<=NR && i<=6;i++) print a[i]; print "total non-bot non-vendor", s}'
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --line-porcelain HEAD -- "$f" | grep '^author-mail ' | sed "s|^author-mail |$f |"; done > /tmp/lines.txt; echo "== all files (vendor included)"; awk '{print $NF}' /tmp/lines.txt | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8; awk '{s++} END{print "total", s}' /tmp/lines.txt; echo "== excluding vendor/ and dependabot"; grep -v '^vendor/' /tmp/lines.txt | grep -v dependabot | awk '{print $NF}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | awk '{s+=$1; a[NR]=$0} END {for(i=1;i<=NR&&i<=6;i++) print a[i]; print "total", s}'; echo "== per file top author (non-vendor)"; grep -v '^vendor/' /tmp/lines.txt | grep -v dependabot | awk '{f=$1; print f, $NF}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k
 - Bash: for a in <email redacted> <email redacted> <email redacted> <email redacted> <email redacted>; do echo "$a last: $(git log -1 --format=%ci --author="$a" HEAD) commits: $(git log --oneline --author="$a" HEAD | wc -l)"; done; git log -1 --format=%ci HEAD
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer: one person owns about half the live code.** Measured by git blame on the 15 tracked files at HEAD, excluding `vendor/` and the dependabot bot:

| Rank | Author (git email) | Live lines | Share | Commits at HEAD | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | <email redacted> | 963 of 1918 | **50.2%** | 201 | 2026-07-23 |
| 2 | <email redacted> | 164 | 8.6% | 4 | 2026-08-24 |
| 3 | <email redacted> | 124 | 6.5% | 1 | 2017-05-23 |
| 4 | <email redacted> | 103 | 5.4% | 1 | 2026-08-10 |
| 5 | <email redacted> | 98 | 5.1% | 1 | 2026-03-04 |
| 6 | <email redacted> | 71 | 3.7% | — | — |

- **Top person:** 50% of live lines, 201 of 300 commits, and the sole owner of the largest files: `color.go` (326 of its lines), `color_test.go` (350), `README.md` (155), and the CI workflow.
- **Next:** no one else holds more than about 9%. The rest is spread across roughly 25 more authors, most with 1 to 4 commits.
- **Vendored code** (`vendor/`, 2 files, 151 lines) is included in the first table's totals but not the second. It is third-party code, so it does not count as the project's ownership.
- **Caveat on the numbers:** blame measures lines that survive today, not knowledge. A mechanical change (such as the `interface{}` → `any` commit) can move line credit. The numbers are a proxy.

**What this means for your risk:** the library is concentrated in one active maintainer. Their last commit is recent (2026-07-23), so this is bus factor 1 for the core, not an orphaned area. The other contributors are one-off or occasional, so they would not cover the core if the maintainer left.

I did not run the busfactor script. It writes `CODEOWNERS` and `ownership.json` into the repo, and you asked for a read-only answer. Its decay-weighted scoring would give a somewhat different ranking, and I can run it with `--dry-run --no-github` if you want that view.
